      "title": "A cash-value policy can offer more than cancellation",
      "narration": "Marcus can no longer afford the continuing premiums on his whole life policy. Before he gives it up, he reviews its nonforfeiture choices. These choices use the value already built under the policy when premium payments stop. The familiar alternatives are taking available cash, using value for extended term insurance, or keeping a smaller amount of paid-up permanent insurance. They preserve different things. A no-cash-value term policy does not suddenly acquire those values because its premium is missed. Start with the actual policy, current values and any outstanding debt. Then compare what protection would remain under each available choice.",
